purchase Arma Colostrum and use my code

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:16.160
May at checkout to get 15% off your

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:18.240
first order. Now, I'm about to give you

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.440
not one, but two methods because maybe

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.880
one of these is going to feel more

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:22.480
natural to you than the other. So, try

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.240
both and keep the one that you like.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.760
Method one is called the scene loop.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.920
This is Neville Goddard's signature

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:29.440
technique. So, as you're lying in bed

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.600
and you feel yourself drifting off to

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.040
sleep, you create one short scene in

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.200
your imagination like a mind movie. That

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:38.520
scene must imply that your wish has

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.560
already been fulfilled. You are at the

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:42.480
end. You're not visualizing yourself

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.960
working towards the goal in your process

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.680
or thinking about the level of effort

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.480
that it takes. You're going to place

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.760
yourself [music] at the ending of that

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.520
movie after you have already have

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:53.440
everything that you wanted, not even the

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.880
moment that you have it, but after that.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.520
Let's say for example, you're

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.440
manifesting a new apartment and you

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:00.040
don't visualize apartment hunting.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.720
You're actually visualizing yourself

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:03.920
standing [music] at your kitchen counter

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.360
on a Tuesday holding onto your coffee

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.400
mug and hearing the sounds of a new

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:09.760
neighborhood. Maybe it's a day just like

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:12.520
this one. The birds are chirping and

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:14.080
it's raining and you feel the fresh air

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.839
on your skin. You're looking outside at

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.120
the view and you feel the texture of

00:11:15.839 --> 00:11:19.760
your floor and how the daylight starts

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:22.520
to hit your face. You [music] play that

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:24.482
scene on a loop over and over again as

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:24.520
you drift off to sleep. And

00:11:24.482 --> 00:11:26.200
>> [music]

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:27.920
>> if your mind wanders off, that's okay,

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:30.200
just bring it back. But the point is you

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:32.360
have to imagine the most mundane and

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:34.440
normal part of your day, which is, you

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:36.440
know, naturally going to be part of your

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:38.440
dream life. And it has to feel so normal

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:40.080
for you. But that scene should also be

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.680
the last thing that your subconscious

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.760
remembers before it takes that scene to

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.440
work for the next 6 to 8 hours. This is

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.480
also what Young would recognize as

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:49.480
active imagination with a specific

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:51.000
directive. You're not passively waiting

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.000
to see what your subconscious mind does

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.000
because you've been doing that your

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.280
whole life. You're basically giving it

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:58.400
directions, like a blueprint in your

00:11:56.280 --> 00:12:00.840
theta state without your gatekeeping

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.040
self-aware conscious mind telling you

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:05.520
that it's unrealistic. Your subconscious

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:07.240
accepts it as an experience rather than

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:09.400
something made up. It is like a

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:10.560
practical real outcome for you. Remember

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:12.840
how your brain doesn't actually

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:14.800
distinguish between a vivid imagination

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.240
and a real one? So you're not actually

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:19.360
pretending anything, but you're

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:21.760
pre-living your wishes as already

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:24.160
fulfilled, done. The second method is

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:26.440
called the sensory shift. So this is for

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.840
everyone who tells me, "May, I literally

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:30.520
cannot visualize anything. My mind is

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:32.840
just blank and I'm having a lot of

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.800
trouble doing this." So I hear you. This

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:36.680
one doesn't actually require you to see

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:38.640
anything. So you're actually already

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:40.160
lying in bed. You feel a mattress

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.920
beneath you, a pillow on your head. You

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.360
feel heavy. So now you don't actually

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.200
need to generate any kind of new

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.320
information. Just reframe whatever

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:49.440
you're already feeling and decide that

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.600
this bed that I'm in is the bed of my

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.240
desired reality. I've already reached my

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.760
destination. So the mattress, for

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:56.800
example, is the mattress in your new

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:58.360
apartment. And the pillow is on the head

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:00.360
of someone who already has what they

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:02.400
want. You sense the room around you and

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:04.920
you decide, "This room that I'm in right

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:06.680
now is my dream room." And you will

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:09.000
imagine that you feel the presence of

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:10.800
whatever you want to represent. So

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.320
Neville Goddard used this method when he

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:14.560
was stationed at a military training

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:16.960
camp during the war and he really wanted

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:18.560
to go home. Every night he laid on that

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.640
camp bed and he felt the mattress

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:22.760
beneath him and he decided, "This is my

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:24.320
bed at home." He imagined his wife

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.800
sleeping next to him. He felt the shape

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:27.680
of his bedroom and he also felt the

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:30.760
presence of his sleeping child. He did

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:32.600
this for 9 days. On the 10th day, he was

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.560
called into the office and they handed

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:36.720
him the discharge papers. You can go

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.280
home now, Neville. So, it only took 10

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:40.400
days for him. And what makes this

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:42.034
technique or method more powerful from a

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.800
psychological perspective is that

00:13:42.034 --> 00:13:45.920
[music] it works with what Freud would

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.120
call the reality principle. In some

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.800
ways, this may actually be more

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:51.000
practical for you. Basically, your

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:52.640
senses are already active and engaged.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.400
You're not fighting your brain to create

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.600
something out of nothing. So, there's

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:58.880
nothing for your active mind to fight

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:00.240
against. You are gently redirecting

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.080
what's already there because you're

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.960
already there in bed. And because these

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:05.560
sensations are real for you, in that the

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:06.960
mattress is real, the pillow's real,

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:09.160
your subconscious mind is more than

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.840
ready to actually accept this reframe.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.760
You're narrowing that gap between the

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:14.320
real and the imagination. So, if you

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:16.360
want to try both methods at the same

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:18.320
time, you can do that, too. Integrating

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:19.760
your beliefs. I want to also circle back

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.200
to where we started because it really

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:22.800
does actually make or break the whole

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:25.520
practice. So, remember when I said that

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:26.760
the reason why most manifestations fail

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:28.080
is because deep down you don't believe

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.680
you can have it. You can loop these

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.080
scenes and do sensory shifting all you

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.960
want. You can practice for a month, a

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:34.680
couple of months, or a few days. But if

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:36.520
underneath all of that, your shadow's

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:38.920
still saying this will never actually

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:41.000
happen, then your subconscious mind

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:43.080
still has that complex. So, Carl Jung

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:45.040
would call this a complex, an

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:47.520
emotionally charged cluster of

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:49.360
associations that basically operate on

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:51.360
its own automatically in the background.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.640
So, these associations that you have are

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:55.400
basically the constant fighting and

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:57.600
resistance between I don't deserve

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:59.320
abundance and I do deserve abundance.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.360
Basically, that will override your

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:03.280
conscious intention unless it's brought

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:05.440
into awareness and integrated. [music]

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:06.839
So, how do you integrate this? Remember,

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:09.280
all of these thoughts that you have that

00:15:06.839 --> 00:15:11.440
are in conflict are part of your shadow.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:13.480
So, try this. Step one, before you do

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:15.000
anything tonight, like other techniques,

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:16.920
sit with yourself for 60 seconds and

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.920
just ask yourself, do I actually believe

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:20.560
this is possible for me? And be really

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:22.000
honest about it. Don't say something

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.560
like, "Yeah, of course I should think

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.920
like that." And actually, be really

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:27.320
honest with yourself. If the answer is

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:28.600
not fully that, that is the awareness of

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:30.080
what you're fighting against. In order

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:31.420
for us to integrate it, we have to first

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.000
acknowledge it. That's why it's step

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:35.320
[music] one. Now, step two, if you

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:37.440
notice resistance, don't fight it and

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:40.200
name it. Say it to yourself quietly or

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:41.720
in your mind, "I notice a part of me

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:43.600
that doesn't believe that this is

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:46.200
possible. I'm not going to argue with

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:48.680
myself, but very gently, I'm going to

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:51.280
show myself a new perspective." This is

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:53.320
shadow work in its most simple and

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.640
rudimentary form. You're not killing

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.960
your doubts, you're not fighting

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.680
yourself. Basically, you're

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:59.600
acknowledging all of these thoughts that

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:02.000
you have that's fighting against you and

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:04.800
you're feeding it and integrating it

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:06.840
into a new possibility, despite what you

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:08.640
may [music] think otherwise. Step three,

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:10.920
start with something your nervous system

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:12.720
can actually accept. If manifesting a

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:14.280
billion dollars feels like a joke to

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.480
you, it will reject that programming.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.600
So, you have to start with something

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:19.160
that creates a slight stretch, but not a

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.880
full snap, just to convince your mind

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:22.280
that it's absolutely possible. Something

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:24.120
that makes you think, "Okay, maybe

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:25.960
that's more realistic and that's fine."

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.880
That is the gateway. [music] It's like

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:30.000
the portal as your subconscious

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:32.440
experiences and small alignments and

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.839
synchronicities come together. I always

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:36.880
try to connect the dots as much as I can

00:16:34.839 --> 00:16:39.120
in my reality just to prove like all of

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:40.760
these synchronicities and coincidences

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:42.880
are not just coincidences because

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.120
literally, your mind goes where your

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:47.400
focus goes and it's the threshold for

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:50.400
what it believes is possible and that

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:52.520
will continue to stretch and expand. So,

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:53.920
try this tonight. Realistically

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:56.160
speaking, maybe half an hour before

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.640
bedtime, put your phone on airplane

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.360
mode, put it in another room, make it

